---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About this site">
  <h1>About this site</h1>

  <h2>Tech stack</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Astro 5.x</strong> for the static-site shell and markdown pipeline.
    Astro was chosen because it is markdown-native (front-matter, MDX, code
    highlight, remark/rehype plugins all built in), ships zero JS by default,
    and hydrates only the interactive widgets ("islands"). Alternatives
    considered were VitePress (forces Vue for widgets) and Docusaurus (heavier
    React dep tree — overkill for a docs site).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Cytoscape.js 3.x</strong> for the interactive graphs. It is
    framework-agnostic (no React/Vue coupling), has good built-in layouts
    (cose, breadthfirst), and pairs cleanly with Astro's island model.
    React Flow was rejected because it would force React into the bundle
    for one widget; d3-force because it requires too much hand-rolled glue.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Mermaid 11.x</strong> for the diagrams embedded in the demo
    markdown. Rendered client-side — the markdown source uses standard
    <code>```mermaid</code> fences and the <code>MermaidRenderer</code>
    island swaps them for SVG after page load.
  </p>

  <h2>Source-of-truth strategy</h2>
  <p>
    The canonical demo content lives in <code>docs/DEMO_*.md</code>. This site
    does <strong>not</strong> duplicate that content; Astro's content collection
    uses a glob loader pointed at <code>../</code> (i.e. <code>docs/</code>
    relative to <code>docs/web/src/content/</code>) so the markdown files
    remain a single source of truth.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <code>docs/DEMO_*.md</code> files landed via
    <a href="https://github.com/NikashPrakash/dot-agents/pull/136" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PR #136</a>
    and are now on <code>master</code>, so local builds work without any staging
    steps.
  </p>

  <h2>What's shipped in this first version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All 5 DEMO pages rendered as styled markdown with sidebar nav, anchors, and code highlight.</li>
    <li>Mermaid block rendering inside demo pages.</li>
    <li>Clickable resource graph: <strong>da resources</strong> (skills, agents, rules, hooks, MCP, scaffolds).</li>
    <li>Clickable graph: <strong>workflow resources</strong> (pr10-branch-split tasks + delegations + lessons).</li>
    <li>Snapshot view: <strong>workspace state</strong> (worktrees + active delegations + eligible queue).</li>
    <li>Tier model diagram (spec → plan → tasks → history) with click-to-expand.</li>
    <li>
      Automated deploy: the site publishes to <a href="https://agorcha.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agorcha.dev</a>
      via a Cloudflare Worker pipeline (<code>.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml</code>).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Stubbed for follow-up</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Lens dispatch diagram.</li>
    <li>Verifier registry / <code>app_type_verifier_map</code> diagram.</li>
    <li>Live JSON ingestion for workspace state (currently a committed snapshot).</li>
    <li>Search across demo pages.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Local development</h2>
  <pre><code>cd docs/web
npm install
npm run dev       # http://localhost:4321
npm run build     # outputs static site to dist/
npm run preview   # serve dist/ to verify</code></pre>
</BaseLayout>
